    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Represents shares transferred by Riva Capital Partners IV, L.P. (&quot;Riva IV&quot;) to Riva IV CV, L.P. (&quot;Riva IV CV&quot;) in connection with an internal restructuring transaction undertaken by Riva IV in which Riva IV formed Riva IV CV.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">Represents the closing price of the Common Stock on October 30, 2026, which was the price used for the transfer from Riva IV to Riva IV CV.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Amount of securities beneficially owned following the reported transaction remains unchanged because each of Riva Capital Management IV, LLC (&quot;RCM IV&quot;), Abrams Capital Management, L.P. (the &quot;LP&quot;) and Abrams Capital Management, LLC (the &quot;LLC&quot;) continue to beneficially own the shares formerly held by Riva IV and now held by Riva IV CV, with such transaction representing a change in the form of beneficial ownership within the meaning of Rule 16a-13 under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, with respect to each of RCM IV, the LP and the LLC.  Riva IV CV has filed a separate Form 3 reporting its acquisition of such shares.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">Shares reported herein as beneficially owned after giving effect to the reported transaction described in footnote 1 above represent 10,930,063 shares held by Abrams Capital Partners II, L.P. (&quot;ACPII&quot;), 11,529,265 shares held by Riva IV CV, 723,761 shares held by Abrams Capital Partners I, L.P. (&quot;ACPI&quot;), 1,232,146 shares held by Whitecrest Partners, LP (&quot;WCP&quot;), 611,820 shares held by Great Hollow International, L.P. (&quot;GHI&quot;), and 7,023,185 shares held by Riva Capital Partners V, L.P. (&quot;Riva V&quot;, and, together with ACPI, ACPII, WCP, GHI, Riva IV and Riva IV CV, collectively the &quot;Abrams Funds&quot;).</footnote>
        <footnote id="F5">Abrams Capital, LLC (&quot;AC LLC&quot;) is the general partner of ACPI, ACPII, and WCP. As a result, AC LLC may be deemed to share voting and dispositive power with respect to the shares held by ACPI, ACPII, and WCP.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F6">RCM IV is the general partner of Riva IV CV and Riva IV. As a result, RCM IV may be deemed to share voting and dispositive power with respect to the shares held by Riva IV and Riva IV CV.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F7">Riva Capital Management V, LLC (&quot;RCM V&quot;) is the general partner of Riva V. As a result, RCM V may be deemed to share voting and dispositive power with respect to the shares held by Riva V.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F8">The LP is the investment manager of each of the Abrams Funds and, in such capacity, manages the investment strategy and decision-making process with respect to investments held by the Abrams Funds. As a result, the LP may be deemed to share voting and dispositive power with respect to the shares held by the Abrams Funds.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F9">The LLC is the general partner of the LP. As a result, the LLC may be deemed to share voting and dispositive power with respect to the shares held by the Abrams Funds.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F10">Each reporting person disclaims beneficial ownership of the reported shares except to the extent of its pecuniary interest therein, and the inclusion of such securities in this report shall not be deemed an admission of beneficial ownership for purposes of Section 16 or for any other purpose.</footnote>
    </footnotes>

